id: pm-gantt-chart-schedule-drift
title: Explain moved goal dates between saved resource schedules
description: Compare saved scheduling inputs with the existing resource scenario engine; prove causes with bounded counterfactual replays and preserve unsupported evidence as gaps.
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-27T05:27:45.157Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T08:14:06.411Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "One estimate change yields exact downstream civil-day delta and causal chain; unchanged rows collapse to references; unsupported inputs remain gaps rather than blamed causes; typed SDK and CLI, bounded TOON/JSON, no-git and public read-only validation."
comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T05:27:48.588Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against current CLI declarations and sibling README surfaces: core owns complete reads, status/relationship registries and serialization; pm-graph snapshot-impact compares topology/frontiers but no calendar allocation or computed schedule dates. Reuse resourceScenarios and its strict duration schema; no new scheduler. Saved snapshots are read-only values, no importer/sync, journal, mutation or shared checkpoint. Attribution uses individual counterfactual reversals; interactions without an individually witnessed effect remain gaps. Native statuses resolve through SDK registry roles before engine projection."
  "2026-10-27T05:40:46.512Z",codex-agent,"Implemented typed snapshot capture, strict snapshot validation and drift SDK plus gantt snapshot/drift CLI commands. Existing engine supplies all dates. One estimate regression proves exact one-day downstream movement and full prerequisite chain. Public origin/main validation: 117 items, 8 active, 9 relationships, 5 missing estimates, 8 missing owners; explicit hypothetical overrides only. Estimate 60 to 540 minutes moved 8 dates, 3 returned, 3 evaluations, zero gaps, 1160 JSON bytes and 1221 TOON bytes. Read-only non-git archive and deterministic replay preserve durable source hashes. Seeded model now varies all native scheduling fields and random custom SDK role registries; read-only feature introduces no mutations, plans, locks, idempotency keys or shared drainer state."
  "2026-10-27T05:44:54.352Z",codex-agent,"Verification: pinned pm linked test runner passed 9/9 tests, including 500 seeded sequences; drift.ts measured 100% lines, branches and functions. Typecheck, lint, zero-duplication and docstring gates pass. Four behavioral reversions were caught: unsupported-baseline comparison, causal replays removed, unchanged collapse removed, and SDK roles replaced by status-name guessing. Source bytes restored after each proof. Inherited resource self-edge throw is tracked separately as pm-gantt-chart-resource-self-prerequisite; drift guards it as an invalid_graph gap. Full npm and Bun release gates will run in CI at unchanged 100/100/100 thresholds."
  "2026-10-27T05:47:06.332Z",codex-agent,"PR 190 is ready for review. Updated the existing exact preflight-owned-command inventory assertion for the two new commands; targeted smoke tests pass. Full release gates are running in CI, and final handoff will cite exact-head results rather than queued or skipped checks."
  "2026-10-27T05:48:58.353Z",codex-agent,"Final input audit tightened unknown-status handling: unresolved SDK roles now stop date replay for that snapshot entirely and retain the exact item ids as gaps. They are never projected to active work, even for a non-attributed date. Focused regressions pass. The existing exact command-scope smoke test also passes 5/5."
  "2026-10-27T06:03:27.455Z",codex-agent,"Final targeted verification: pinned pm test --run --progress --timeout 300 passed 10/10 tests with zero failures/skips/cancellations; drift.ts is 100% lines, branches and functions. Default 120-second linked-test timeout was exceeded under host contention without an assertion failure; the serial rerun completed in 230 seconds. Route graphs are now computed once per edit, only over active scheduled tasks, in stable code-unit order; the maximum 200-active-task calendar test reports all 199 moved finishes using 3 evaluations. All 5 packed install scenarios passed locally (npm/npx, Bun/bunx, minimum host, npm global, Bun global), each proving an exact 1-day drift. No full local suite was run; full npm/Bun release evidence remains the CI gate."
  "2026-10-27T06:07:25.018Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed the installed host is pm CLI 2026.10.26 and searched its public SDK scheduling/calendar/graph declarations: no schedule-scenario drift comparison or resource allocator overlap. The CI packed matrix now tests npm-global and Bun-global against that actual deployed consumer version; development/minimum SDK remains pinned at 2026.10.20. Earlier local five-scenario packed receipt used the pinned host throughout; the expanded consumer-version proof is delegated to the required CI release gate."
  "2026-10-27T06:19:56.391Z",codex-agent,"CI run 40459301636 executed 373/373 passing tests on Node 22.18 and Node 26, with zero failures/skips/cancellations, but correctly rejected 99.80% index.ts branch coverage (100% for drift.ts and every other measured source). Added real SDK harness executions of successful snapshot/drift handlers, oversized input and scalar JSON so the source module measures the paths already proven by the packed subprocess. Focused packed regression passes; LCOV shows zero missed branches in both new handlers and their file helpers. No production code or coverage threshold changed; full gates will rerun at the new head."
  "2026-10-27T07:19:05.751Z",codex-agent,"Re-review round 1 confirmed both findings. General rules: every successful replayable producer must fit its consumer transport, and untrusted dictionary names must access own entries only (never Object.prototype values or setters). Fresh fetch shows branch contains origin/main (6 ahead, 0 behind); worktree initially clean. Supplied review and GitHub review comments contain no additional non-blocking findings. Class audit covers snapshot SDK/CLI and JSON/TOON envelopes, resource work/calendar dictionaries, uncertainty overrides, schema dispatch tables, and all bounded JSON command readers. Preserve existing control/estimate file caps, add a larger saved-snapshot file cap plus schema-owned producer byte budget, centralize bounded descriptor-based reads, and test prototype names and producer round trips adversarially across SDK, non-git CLI and packed npm/Bun consumers."
  "2026-10-27T07:38:25.547Z",codex-agent,"Both review classes are fixed and adversarial focused tests pass 4/4. The shared schema caps canonical pretty snapshot JSON at 4 MiB; saved-file replay allows 16 MiB including host envelopes/indentation, while controls retain 256 KiB and estimates 64 KiB. All three CLI file paths share a bounded UTF-8 descriptor reader with read-time growth checks and guaranteed close. Calendar/work lookups and schema dispatch use own entries; counterfactual dictionaries reconstruct through Map/Object.fromEntries, preserving prototype-named keys without setters. Existing uncertainty own-entry guards were already correct; fixed status tables and generated brand tokens are trusted closed enums, not user-key dictionaries. No extra non-blocking findings were supplied. Six function-level reversions were caught: old snapshot file cap, missing producer byte cap, missing read-growth check, inherited shared lookup, inherited calendar lookup, and prototype-setter reconstruction. Each failed with ERR_ASSERTION and original source bytes were restored. Tests cover 500 producer transports, 500 prototype-name sequences, complete 2000-item non-git replay and all command reader bounds; packed matrix now exercises those same large envelopes and constructor/__proto__ calendars."
  "2026-10-27T08:08:42.206Z",codex-agent,"Review completion: isolated-identity full npm run release:check AND bun run release:check passed serially with a two-worker cap. Each ran 377/377 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todo, and measured 9 sources at 100% lines/branches/functions. Both five-scenario packed matrices passed: development/minimum host 2026.10.20 plus npm/Bun global consumers 2026.10.26, every replay containing 2000 items and constructor/__proto__ calendars (567363-byte envelope), every estimate drift exactly 1 day. The SDK producer regression itself measures 370236 compact bytes / 566672 pretty-envelope bytes. Final fetch found one main commit changing only Hound configuration and a separate tracker item; integrate that main commit before pushing, retaining main history byte prefixes. CI will revalidate the final merged head. Both supplied findings are addressed; no supplied non-blocking findings remain."
  "2026-10-27T08:14:06.410Z",codex-agent,"Integrated origin/main 9857eb2 via merge ffc6895 after fixing the review in 1600105. Main changed only Hound configuration and its separate tracker item; no product source changed in the merge. Verified every existing main history is a byte prefix of the branch history. Strict pm health passes under isolated CI identity, core tracker health passes, and regenerated changelog check passes. Default local health reports an unrelated global pm-github SDK-host skew (20 versus 26) that disappears with isolated identity; no SDK dependency bump or history repair was performed. Local npm/Bun full release receipts remain 377/377 each, nine measured sources at 100/100/100 and five successful 2000-item packed consumers each. Final exact-head CI results are linked through PR 190 checks."
